{"event_type":"review","id":"85f0004d088caac3ed9698548f6f9af749ad3487fb87c5c974c2ac9410253a35","occurred_at":"2026-11-05T21:18:54Z","payload":{"artifacts":[{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/5a069ddcc79bdf6b73d12999343647d6bec2dfe91db75fe75fb04e822edbe165","sha256":"5a069ddcc79bdf6b73d12999343647d6bec2dfe91db75fe75fb04e822edbe165"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1af8e8b0e7a515ddf4567ab7d14538e5ce0b20cf1dd9182339cf43fffd21f768","sha256":"1af8e8b0e7a515ddf4567ab7d14538e5ce0b20cf1dd9182339cf43fffd21f768"},{"kind":"git-bundle","location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/cdff321f12aaf6e1921d6498c72b13a815d20e4c9c14c1fa1845830c7e79736c","sha256":"cdff321f12aaf6e1921d6498c72b13a815d20e4c9c14c1fa1845830c7e79736c"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/767519e066bd89f46b9237f1c0750758246e55791e0f9da5e89645a49ff3aa41","sha256":"767519e066bd89f46b9237f1c0750758246e55791e0f9da5e89645a49ff3aa41"},{"location":"/home/ctaylor/.local/share/crq-backfill/artifacts/sha256/1cb04c7be6b496110fd592eeeda63b2a9ab5fbddf06a0581e8e7aac4b5216499","sha256":"1cb04c7be6b496110fd592eeeda63b2a9ab5fbddf06a0581e8e7aac4b5216499"}],"attempt_id":"495bbca775ee9118811279d2d2bd6b147d4f49f58374b9f05cdbb852239f7d16:0:1","base":"fd6f1190d9305e6acf56715e1be16cf41c4e0bb4","completion":{"errors":[],"exit_code":0,"scope_verified":true,"skipped":false,"terminal":true},"findings":[{"anchor_status":"unverified","blob":"05ef0264fb9bb97d6b0ea458960d63ff30103a54","body":"**Reject a non-finite or negative `maxRetries` in `executeMerges`.**\n\n`maxRetries` is read without a range check at `src/ops/merge/executeMerges.ts:179`. The retry stop condition at line 279 is `attempt >= maxRetries`. If `maxRetries` is `NaN`, that comparison is always `false`. If it is `Infinity`, it never becomes `true`. A forge that keeps reporting \"base branch was modified\" can then retry without a limit, as long as the head and base do not change. This breaks the contract in the file header (lines 53-55): at most `maxRetries + 1` `mergePr` calls per action.\n\nThe dispatch path already rejects these values. `ExecuteMergesInputSchema` in `src/ops/merge/registry.ts:310` uses `z.number().int().min(0)`, and the registry importer forwards `maxRetries` only after that validation. Direct TypeScript callers of the exported `executeMerges` are not covered, because the `number` type allows `NaN` and `Infinity`. Validating inside the op keeps the bound for those callers.\n\n<details>\n<summary>🛡️ Proposed fix</summary>\n\n```diff\n-  const maxRetries = input.maxRetries ?? DEFAULT_MAX_RETRIES;\n+  const requested = input.maxRetries ?? DEFAULT_MAX_RETRIES;\n+  if (!Number.isSafeInteger(requested) || requested < 0) {\n+    throw new RangeError(\n+      `executeMerges: maxRetries must be a non-negative integer, got ${String(requested)}`,\n+    );\n+  }\n+  const maxRetries = requested;\n```\n\n</details>","id":"91966102630f49a789943516c5d8d436349fe732391087ae93150fe9d1b4012e","intervals":[],"path":"src/ops/merge/executeMerges.ts","severity":"minor","source_id":null,"status":"untriaged","title":"Reject a non-finite or negative `maxRetries` in `executeMerges`."}],"head":"bc69e477eaa75b58edfeb0604d063e305e1aa2e2","head_tree":"013c2fa4bf520f2358e9d1367a3d73c21ab4fb44","input_scope":[{"blob":"ef8414b9dfb85190b526632a78a55e35087fc3ea","intervals":[[1,59]],"path":"src/ops/merge/diagnoseMergeFailure.ts"},{"blob":"05ef0264fb9bb97d6b0ea458960d63ff30103a54","intervals":[[1,542]],"path":"src/ops/merge/executeMerges.ts"},{"blob":"7d4ae6cbb19cfcba038865f1f6a1a351c54c5660","intervals":[[1,10],[23,55]],"path":"src/ops/merge/index.ts"},{"blob":"cf304f9decc43cd52d654ee52195bc02e6dbb441","intervals":[[1,1798]],"path":"test/ops/merge/executeMerges.test.ts"}],"job_id":"495bbca775ee9118811279d2d2bd6b147d4f49f58374b9f05cdbb852239f7d16:0","outcome":"completed","paths":[{"baseline":{"entry":null,"merge":"5f4216dd116